From: EVE build <builder@projecteve.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] aot: parse the kernel BTF before running the program

The AOT runtime constructs BPFtrace and runs the loaded program without
the parse_btf() call the bpftrace binary makes first; run() then hands
*btf_ to every AttachedProbe. With a null pointer that is undefined
behaviour the Alpine builds got away with; Ubuntu builds libstdc++ with
assertions enabled and bpftrace-aotrt aborts in unique_ptr::operator*
before the first probe is attached.

--- a/src/aot/aot_main.cpp
+++ b/src/aot/aot_main.cpp
@@ -115,6 +115,7 @@ int main(int argc, char* argv[])
     return 1;
 
   BPFtrace bpftrace(std::move(output));
+  bpftrace.parse_btf({});
   int err = aot::load(bpftrace, argv[optind]);
   if (err)
   {
